  {
    "id": "ada76c80-2c04-5e6c-83c6-f67377fbf0be",
    "pack": "npc-core",
    "kind": "spell",
    "slug": "spell:infiltrators-tunnel",
    "name": "Infiltrator's Tunnel",
    "level": 4,
    "rarity": "rare",
    "traits": ["concentrate", "manipulate", "teleportation"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "npc-core"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "It's best to know the ingress and egress points for any location you plan to rob. But it's even better to make your own! You create two portals. One appears on a flat surface you can touch, and the other appears on a different flat surface in range that you can see."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "You can move through the portals as though they were adjacent to each other. Any other creature attempting to move through the portals must succeed at a Will saving throw or be teleported up to 30 feet away from their starting point to a random safe space determined by the GM."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Heightened (6th)",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " When you Cast the Spell, you can designate up to 5 other creatures to freely move between the portals."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
